_count":3,"retweet_count":8},"text":"My WSJ China newsletter column made it into the print edition of today’s @WSJ — a first! After a couple of years of writing this column, seeing it in print feels like a special moment. Grateful to subscribers who’ve followed along and to the editors who made it happen. 🗞️ https://t.co/Ml3Kn4OOcC https://t.co/J9glEbQE5L","url":"https://x.com/Lingling_Wei/status/2112968586079744448"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112963399785037824"]},"author_id":"48463418","created_at":"2026-10-21T17:45:06.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112963402867826768"],"entities":{"urls":[{"description":"The origin of the solar corona's million Kelvin temperatures remains a central unsolved problem. While the nanoflare hypothesis is widely accepted and describes magnetic reconnection events at coronal current sheets that are slowly formed by complex driver flows at the solar surface, the possibility remains that macroscopic fluid instabilities self-organize microscale current sheets where none previously existed. We present the first laboratory demonstration that the Rayleigh-Taylor instability self-organizes antiparallel magnetic fields, driving reconnection at ${r}_{\\mathrm{max}}\\ensuremath{\\approx}0.078$ that heats electrons to ${T}_{e}\\ensuremath{\\approx}70.8\\ifmmode\\pm\\else\\textpm\\fi{}6.5\\text{ }\\text{ }\\mathrm{eV}$, twice that of shock-dominated cases. Radiative magnetohydrodynamic simulations confirm Joule heating dominates viscous dissipation. Despite differing global energy storage, our dimensionless parameters (${R}_{m}\\ensuremath{\\approx}3\\ifmmode\\times\\else\\texttimes\\fi{}{1","display_url":"go.aps.org/3VUfRG5","end":233,"expanded_url":"https://go.aps.org/3VUfRG5","start":210,"status":200,"title":"Laboratory Demonstration of Coronal Heating via Magnetic Reconnection during Nanoflares","unwound_url":"https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/tmll-l58c","url":"https://t.co/rSBNHJ1Ts4"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/qDk6XiMcjG","end":257,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/APSphysics/status/2112963402867826768/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112963399785037824","start":234,"url":"https://t.co/qDk6XiMcjG"}]},"id":"2112963402867826768","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":5,"impression_count":1099,"like_count":13,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":3},"text":"Why is the sun's corona millions of degrees hotter than its surface? A study in Physical Review Letters used powerful lasers to recreate solar nanoflares in the lab and watch them heat plasma.\n\nRead the study: https://t.co/rSBNHJ1Ts4 https://t.co/qDk6XiMcjG","url":"https://x.com/APSphysics/status/2112963402867826768"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112962637281873920"]},"author_id":"702235316812275712","created_at":"2026-10-21T17:42:10.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112962663974350883"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/jcNlmT0h4x","end":275,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2112962663974350883/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112962637281873920","start":252,"url":"https://t.co/jcNlmT0h4x"}]},"id":"2112962663974350883","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":1097,"like_count":7,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":1},"text":"Here's a long-run view of the compression in pay across educational attainment:\n\nPremium for advanced degrees and penalty for not finishing HS shrinking meaningfully; not much change to middle rungs (HS diploma all the way to 4 year bachelor's degree) https://t.co/jcNlmT0h4x","url":"https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2112962663974350883"},{"author_id":"14096763","created_at":"2026-10-21T17:12:38.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112955228945539495"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/OblomovBukowsk…","end":303,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/OblomovBukowsky/status/2112837101108728136","start":280,"url":"https://t.co/wYlS91by9k"}]},"id":"2112955228945539495","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":20,"impression_count":20885,"like_count":169,"quote_count":4,"r